Here is the commit message:
SOLR-7411: fix threadsafety bug in SearchHandler introduced
 in SOLR-7380

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/dev/trunk@1674163 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by a lack of proper thread-safety in the handling of the `components` variable within the `SearchHandler` class. Specifically, the `components` variable was not declared as volatile, which could lead to inconsistent views of the variable across different threads. This could result in one thread seeing a null value while another thread was in the process of initializing it, leading to potential race conditions and unpredictable behavior.

Here is the patch:
